From 7f292b4813d000f7bc83a1535ec7f3d18170e987 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium Dev <dev@pandemonium.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:23:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] feat(sim_api,sim): expose fog tiles and own production
 queues in PlayerView
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

M10-prep review finding: the boundary carried no fog or queue data, so the
client could not draw the fog of war (plan §11.2's fog visualization) or
build §11.4's production queue display — it rendered the full snapshot,
which leaks hidden entities to the human the same way the AI is forbidden
to see them.

PlayerView gains two fields:
- fog: the player's per-tile three-state fog row (TileFog, row-major in
  the map's own tile order), mirrored from the stage-9 fog cache. Derived
  state like the fog itself (A-059) — the canonical hash is untouched and
  all golden pins hold.
- production: the player's own queues (QueueView: producer, items with
  per-item progress_milli, rally point), producers ascending by id, empty
  queues included so a command card can see an idle producer. Fog hides
  enemy production exactly as it hides enemy entities.

AI parity is structural: both fields flow through the same PlayerView the
AI already reads — the same information is available to every issuer
(FD-7/FD-8), the AI simply need not use it.

Pinned by two new sim tests: fog tiles in map order (visible under own
units, hidden past vision, empty for absent slots) and own-queue exposure
with monotonic progress_milli and enemy queues filtered.
