From f1fa1f4a488f673f2c33cbab12eb9d7851b10a23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium Dev <dev@pandemonium.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:54:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] feat(client): blob shadows and ground-projected
 selection rings

The M9.1 selection cue was screen-space corner brackets; nothing anchored
the entities to the ground - the silhouettes floated over the terrain
like unplaced icons. This pass adds a ground decal pipeline: instanced,
alpha-blended geometry laid flat on the ground plane, depth-tested with
writes off (LESS-equal) plus a small lift, so decals hug the terrain and
never z-fight with it or the fog.

- Blob shadow under every entity (one dark ellipse, sized to the
  silhouette's ground radius - a command center casts more shadow than a
  worker).
- Selection rings become Generals-style ground ellipses in own-team
  green under the selected, riding a hair above the shadow plane.
- One pipeline, two geometry streams (unit quad, 24-segment annulus) and
  one shared instance buffer drawn in two instance ranges - no new bind
  groups, no per-decal draw-call churn.
- build_shadows / build_rings are pure and unit-tested: one shadow per
  entity, rings only under the selected, ring-above-shadow layering,
  size ordering by kind.
