From e84ee41c1513214b6d9025d192a100dc25b09096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium Dev <dev@pandemonium.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:57:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] feat(client): death fades - the battlefield registers
 its losses
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Entities popped out of existence the tick they died (the interpolator
drops them, by design). A battle read as a coin-flip: units vanished
with no weight. Deaths now leave a short fade at the entity's last-seen
spot: the silhouette's main mass sinks, shrinks to a quarter, and chars
toward soot over ~14 presented frames (plan §11.5's death fade, event
driven - the Died event fires it, the client's last-seen table supplies
