From 048bc8a7357bb629a4f6e2edb245da922de5b968 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium Dev <dev@pandemonium.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:22:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] feat(engine,client): the minimap - fog, entity dots,
 viewport, click-to-move
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plan §11.4's minimap was never built; a player who lost sight of a fight
had no instrument but scrolling around. This adds the full panel:

- A map-sized RGBA texture composited on the CPU every frame: the baked
  per-tile terrain base (from the terrain mesh's own shaded palette),
  fog darkening layered from the PlayerView's encoding (hidden tiles go
  near-black, explored half-dark, visible clear), and one team-tinted
  dot per visible entity. One small texture upload per frame, one quad.
- The camera viewport indicator: the frustum's ground footprint (new
  RtsCamera::ground_footprint_corners - presentation math with the
  shallow-pitch clamp documented) mapped to panel pixels and drawn as a
  dotted outline that rotates with the camera yaw.
- Click-to-move-camera (left-click focuses, preserving zoom) and
  right-click orders at the mapped ground point - Move, or AttackMove
  when armed, so the minimap is a command surface, not just a map.
- The engine camera test pins the footprint's pitch behavior (steep
  views stay near the target; shallow views see more ground).
