The acceptance list (plan §13 A4) named add-a-map with the same pattern
as A3, but no such test existed - the sweep would have hit an honest
gap. The runtime half now lives beside A3 in the content pipeline suite:

- A fresh 48x48 map (rock spine, two starts, two ore nodes, and a small
  display-only heightmap exercising the schema-v2 path) is written into
  a copy of the content tree, replacing the Alpha map; the bundle loads,
  the map id moves, the rock spine is impassable in the sim's
  passability grid, both nodes spawn from data, and the heightmap rides
  along as display-only data.
- The simulation runs on it: the starting worker accepts and completes a
  Move across the new map.
- The commit carrying this test shows zero diffs under crates/sim/ - the
  git-diff half of the criterion, per the A3 fixture protocol.
