Subject: [PATCH 09/10] feat(tools): honest soak telemetry + the plan's real
 stuck threshold
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The M10 soak evidence run exposed two defects in the M10-prep tooling:

- end-tick telemetry reported the tick BUDGET, not the match's end: the
  runner deliberately keeps simulating to its budget after MatchEnded
  fires (the M7 'ran the budget without crashing' contract), so the
  replay's last checkpoint is always the budget. MatchSummary now
  records the tick MatchEnded fired, and the soak reads it — a resolved
  match reports its real end, only a budgeted-out match reports the
  budget.
- the default budget (18000 ticks / 10 game-minutes) was half the plan's
  own A7 stuck threshold (20 minutes = 36000 ticks), while the M9 sweep
  measured legitimate matches resolving as late as tick ~23300 — the
  old default miscounted 4 of 32 matches as stuck (87.5% 'resolution
  rate' where the truth was 100%). The default is now 36000.

Evidence with the fixed tool (release, 32 seeds from 0): 32/32 resolved,
0 crashed, avg end tick 11877, max 23265 — consistent with the M9
alpha-loop sweep.
